From: Kevin Liu <11365056+kliu128@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: nss: do not invert the mesh forwarding setting

When user space sets dot11MeshForwarding, mac80211 stores the value in
bss_conf.nss_offld_mesh_forward_enabled and ath11k copies it unchanged into
the firmware's block_mesh_forwarding field. Enabling forwarding therefore
tells the NSS firmware to block it: a mesh point configured with
mesh_fwding=1 peers and carries its own traffic, but relays nothing
between its peers.

Seen on three IPQ5018 units in a line (TP-Link Deco XE5300, NSS firmware
12.5): with "option mesh_fwding '1'" on the middle node the two-hop path
resolved and no frame passed; without the option, or with the middle node
on the host path, it did.

---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
@@ -1957,7 +1957,7 @@ int ath11k_nss_mesh_config_update(struct
 
 	if (changed & BSS_CHANGED_NSS_MESH_FWD_ENABLED) {
 		nss_msg->block_mesh_forwarding =
-			vif->bss_conf.nss_offld_mesh_forward_enabled;
+			!vif->bss_conf.nss_offld_mesh_forward_enabled;
 		nss->mesh_forward_enabled =
 			vif->bss_conf.nss_offld_mesh_forward_enabled;
 		nss_msg->config_flags |= NSS_WIFI_MESH_CONFIG_FLAG_BLOCK_MESH_FWD_VALID;
